<newsitem itemid="62642" id="root" date="1996-09-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Hunting provisions push H1 results into loss.</title>
<headline>Hunting provisions push H1 results into loss.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>6 months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		32.1 loss	    vs 5.7 profit</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 Nil		    vs 4.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     14.2 loss	    vs 15 profit</p>
<p> Turnover		   628		    vs 566</p>
<p>NOTE - Hunting Plc said results were hit by exceptional provisions of 40.5 million stg to cover problems in the aviation unit, namely for cost overruns on interiors for the Bombardier Dash-8 and for a 10.5 million stg writeoff on its investment in the poor-selling British Aerospace Jetstream 41 turboprop.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 16.7 loss	    vs 19.0</p>
<p> Exceptional provision  40.5 loss	    vs none</p>
<p> Interest payable	 4.5		    vs 4.0</p>
<p> Tax			  4.2		    vs 4.9</p>
<p> Net taxed		  18.4 loss	    vs 10.1 profit</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
